  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, most assets built with non-graph compilers (i.e. U#) require that the compiler be present, and inject a bunch of C# into your project. This is both a security risk (because you're pulling in editor extensions which can do whatever they like) and a usability issue (you need to pull in a rather large asset, and even if you do want to use U#, your compilation times keep growing as you add assets).\nIt would be nice to be able to compile this U# code and distribute just the compiled asset. This is _almost_ possible today, but needs a bit more support to be possible without the need for editor scripting to load the compiled code.\nIn particular, what is needed is a subtype of UdonProgramAsset, distributed as part of the VRCSDK, which:\n1. Serializes the program within the ProgramAsset (the current UdonProgramAsset does not do this, and needs to be subclassed to be usable)\n2. Hides the default disassembly view in the inspector\n3. Provides a public function to set the contents based on an IUdonProgram, or a SerializedUdonProgramAsset.\nToday, if you wanted to do this precompiled asset distribution, you'd still need your own subclass of UdonProgramAsset that extracts the serialized program from the source SerializedUdonProgramAsset and shoves it into its own fields, and then loads it back later; editor extensions aren't quite avoidable today.",
